; `nth` and `count` — the two list readers outside the higher-order
; binder forms, and the only core functions that turn a vector back into
; a scalar without arithmetic.
;
; `nth` is 0-indexed (form 0 reads the first element, form 1 the last),
; and an out-of-range index is a runtime error rather than a nil: form 2
; produces a diagnostic and no value, which is why no `:index 2` entry
; follows. `count` of an empty vector is 0, not an error.
(nth [10 20 30] 0)
(nth [10 20 30] 2)
(nth [10 20 30] 9)
(count [1 2 3 4])
(count [])
